  "name": "Lean Mass: 6 Week Workout Program to Build Lean Muscle",
  "weeks": 6,
  "daysPerWeek": 4,
  "description": "Four weekly sessions for legs, chest and biceps, back, then shoulders and triceps, using a 2/0/2 tempo.",
  "goals": [
    "muscle"
  ],
  "level": "intermediate",
  "equipment": [
    "barbell",
    "bench",
    "bodyweight",
    "cable",
    "dumbbells",
    "machine"
  ],
  "schedule": "Repeat the four ordered training days each week for six weeks. The article does not prescribe weekdays or placement of rest days.",
  "progression": "No fixed weekly load increase or RIR/RPE is prescribed. The author recommends a deload week after the six-week block; it is guidance outside the six training weeks.",
  "notes": "Source duration: 30–45 minutes. Use a 2/0/2 tempo; rest 30–60s between sets and exercises, with 45s recommended and used as the editable default. Warm-up counts and loads are unspecified. Unilateral rep counts are retained as printed; no extra per-side convention is inferred. Incline press, seated military press and preacher curl variants follow the linked barbell exercise guides.",
